  "review_notes": [
    "prolong his days: the לוֹ is read under rule 40, the preposition unrepresented and the suffix taking the possessive pronoun written for it, as rule 40 gives the thee of לֶךְ־לְךָ to the suffix and as 8.7 and 8.15 are read. Fusing the pair under rules 30 and 49 was the competing reading and is rejected because rule 49's genitive governs a לְ that is itself a verbless clause's predicate. The italic days remains a supplied object with no morpheme to answer to.",
    "מִלִּפְנָיו is a three-morpheme fusion on one English word, headed on פָּנֶה, which is the morpheme whose lexeme the word writes."
  ]
